+
+WP-07 batch order follows the **actual dependency graph**, not this example list:
+compact independent products (Automotive, Finance, Weekly Review); household
+products and bots; Health/nutrition/Fitness; Piano/game experiences; School and
+remaining content-heavy products. Existing cycles or shared writers are resolved
+before their batch. The full primary source inventory is in scope, not just
+these named examples. Do not declare the migration complete after the pilot.
+
+For each move: capture pre-move tests/exports → establish public seams → relocate
+implementation/tests/assets once → update every consumer and registration → run
+focused positive and negative tests → reconcile inventory → review the diff for
+logic changes. Any behavior fix is a separate commit and approval item. Stable
+external APIs may remain aliases by design; old private source paths may not.
